 "result_text": "`get_bucket_location` should now raise the stubbed client error instead of the `AttributeError`. I haven't run the issue's example or any tests.\n\nThe fix is in `parse_get_bucket_location` in `botocore/handlers.py`. That handler already returned early when a stub had pre-filled `LocationConstraint`. It now also returns early when the parsed response contains an `Error` key, which is what `add_client_error` produces. Otherwise it tried to read `http_response.content` from a response that doesn't exist, and that caused the crash.\n\nA real HTTP error response would also skip the XML parsing now. Error responses carry an `Error` key too, so the normal error-handling path should still raise the `ClientError`.\n\nbotocore reported that `handlers.py` changed on disk after my edit. I didn't see what changed, so I haven't checked whether the change affects this fix.",
